Z||000027||filthyscarecrow||06-23-2001||01:41 AM||||2 things i learned at skip barber:<BR>1. racing games make piss poor driving schools. <BR>2. if it's totally gone, you lost it, and there's no going back, wait til the car is spinning in the direction that the road goes and LOCK THE DAMN BRAKES! lock all four wheels. slide straight. a car sliding sideways will come to a halt pretty damn quickly without hitting anything. obviously though, locking them at the right time takes concentration. <BR>i'd be willing to bet that your tire pressures were off. if you've gone through there lots of times before and nothing happened but it jumped out on you this time, i think you might not have had even tire pressures. <BR>fieros are nightmares to drive though if you don't know what you're doing. i bet half the reason pontiac really stopped making them was that stupid sorority girls bought them because they look cute (all my girlfriends say my car is cute) and didn't have a f-ing clue how to drive them and tried to carry the brakes into the corner in the rain and ended up hugging a telephone pole, thus startign the legal snowball of insurance claims and what not and pontiac realised that the american public was ill equipped to handle such a piece of machinery. lemme ask you this, how many of us have managed to spin on dry pavement? (and a rear bar will only make the condition worse, not better. i'm not sure what whoever is was that said that was thinking. a rear bar will induce more oversteer, not reduce it...) ||||reg||1
